a nonzero offset delta not in D adds every edge (x,0)-(y,1) with x XOR y =
delta.  Removing an offset delta in D deletes every such edge.  For nonzero
delta this is exactly 16 ordinary edge editions: both orientations of
each of 8 unordered base pairs.  Thus at most
32 ordinary edge editions are allowed.

